{"id":"pt_text_brecht_lebensreglen","title_original":"Brecht, An die Nachgeborenen","title_ja":"ブレヒト「後の世代へ」","author_name_display":"Bertolt Brecht","era_year":1939,"era_period":"独語モダン","culture_region":"20-21世紀グローバル","language_original":"de","form_genre":"自由詩","length_lines":3,"full_text_or_excerpt":"Wirklich, ich lebe in finsteren Zeiten!\nDas arglose Wort ist töricht.","public_domain_status":"fair-use-excerpt","source_url":"https://de.wikisource.org/","source_archive":"批評対象範囲","canonical_tier":1},
{"id":"pt_text_walcott_omeros","title_original":"Walcott, Omeros","title_ja":"ウォルコット『オメロス』","author_name_display":"Derek Walcott","era_year":1990,"era_period":"カリブ・モダン","culture_region":"20-21世紀グローバル","language_original":"en","form_genre":"叙事詩","length_lines":3,"full_text_or_excerpt":"This is how, one sunrise, we cut down them canoes.\nPhiloctete smiles for the tourists","public_domain_status":"fair-use-excerpt","source_url":"https://www.poetryfoundation.org/","source_archive":"批評対象範囲","canonical_tier":1},
{"id":"pt_text_heaney_bog","title_original":"Heaney, Bogland","title_ja":"ヒーニー「沼地」","author_name_display":"Seamus Heaney","era_year":1969,"era_period":"アイルランド・モダン","culture_region":"20-21世紀グローバル","language_original":"en","form_genre":"抒情詩","length_lines":3,"full_text_or_excerpt":"We have no prairies\nTo slice a big sun at evening—\nEverywhere the eye concedes to","public_domain_status":"fair-use-excerpt","source_url":"https://www.poetryfoundation.org/","source_archive":"批評対象範囲","canonical_tier":1},
{"id":"pt_text_tagore_103","title_original":"Tagore, Gitanjali #103","title_ja":"タゴール『ギーターンジャリ』第103詩","author_name_display":"Rabindranath Tagore","era_year":1910,"era_period":"近代ベンガル","culture_region":"20-21世紀グローバル","language_original":"en","form_genre":"散文詩","length_lines":3,"full_text_or_excerpt":"In one salutation to thee, my God, let all my senses spread out and touch this world at thy feet.","public_domain_status":"PD-original","source_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/files/7164/","source_archive":"Project Gutenberg","canonical_tier":1},
{"id":"pt_text_naidu_palanquin","title_original":"Naidu, Palanquin Bearers","title_ja":"サロジニ・ナイドゥ「駕籠夫」","author_name_display":"Sarojini Naidu","era_year":1905,"era_period":"近代インド","culture_region":"20-21世紀グローバル","language_original":"en","form_genre":"抒情詩","length_lines":4,"full_text_or_excerpt":"Lightly, O lightly we bear her along,\nShe sways like a flower in the wind of our song;\nShe skims like a bird on the foam of a stream,\nShe floats like a laugh from the lips of a dream","public_domain_status":"PD-original","source_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/","source_archive":"Project Gutenberg","canonical_tier":1},
{"id":"pt_text_aurobindo_savitri","title_original":"Sri Aurobindo, Savitri","title_ja":"オーロビンド『サーヴィトリー』","author_name_display":"Sri Aurobindo","era_year":1950,"era_period":"近代インド","culture_region":"20-21世紀グローバル","language_original":"en","form_genre":"叙事詩","length_lines":3,"full_text_or_excerpt":"It was the hour before the Gods awake.\nAcross the path of the divine Event\nThe huge foreboding mind of Night, alone","public_domain_status":"fair-use-excerpt","source_url":"https://www.poetryfoundation.org/","source_archive":"批評対象範囲","canonical_tier":2},
{"id":"pt_text_aime_cesaire_cahier","title_original":"Césaire, Cahier d'un retour au pays natal","title_ja":"セゼール『帰郷ノート』","author_name_display":"Aimé Césaire","era_year":1939,"era_period":"ネグリチュード","culture_region":"20-21世紀グローバル","language_original":"fr","form_genre":"自由詩","length_lines":3,"full_text_or_excerpt":"Au bout du petit matin, sur cette plus fragile épaisseur de terre que dépasse de façon humiliante son grandiose avenir","public_domain_status":"fair-use-excerpt","source_url":"https://fr.wikisource.org/","source_archive":"批評対象範囲","canonical_tier":1},
{"id":"pt_text_senghor_femme","title_original":"Senghor, Femme noire","title_ja":"サンゴール「黒い女」","author_name_display":"Léopold Sédar Senghor","era_year":1945,"era_period":"ネグリチュード","culture_region":"20-21世紀グローバル","language_original":"fr","form_genre":"抒情詩","length_lines":3,"full_text_or_excerpt":"Femme nue, femme noire\nVêtue de ta couleur qui est vie, de ta forme qui est beauté!","public_domain_status":"fair-use-excerpt","source_url":"https://fr.wikisource.org/","source_archive":"批評対象範囲","canonical_tier":1},
{"id":"pt_text_okot_lawino_2","title_original":"p'Bitek, Song of Lawino, Ch.2","title_ja":"オコット『ラウィーノの歌』第2章","author_name_display":"Okot p'Bitek","era_year":1966,"era_period":"アフリカ独立後","culture_region":"アフリカ","language_original":"ach","form_genre":"叙事詩","length_lines":3,"full_text_or_excerpt":"Husband, listen!\nI am tired of all this fighting.\nI no longer want to live this way","public_domain_status":"fair-use-excerpt","source_url":"https://www.poetryfoundation.org/","source_archive":"批評対象範囲","canonical_tier":1},
{"id":"pt_text_diop_afrique","title_original":"David Diop, Afrique","title_ja":"ダヴィッド・ジョップ「アフリカ」","author_name_display":"David Diop","era_year":1956,"era_period":"ネグリチュード","culture_region":"アフリカ","language_original":"fr","form_genre":"抒情詩","length_lines":4,"full_text_or_excerpt":"Afrique mon Afrique\nAfrique des fiers guerriers dans les savanes ancestrales\nAfrique que chante ma grand-mère\nAu bord de son fleuve lointain","public_domain_status":"fair-use-excerpt","source_url":"https://fr.wikisource.org/","source_archive":"批評対象範囲","canonical_tier":1},
{"id":"pt_text_okigbo_heaven","title_original":"Okigbo, Heavensgate","title_ja":"クリストファー・オキグボ『天国の門』","author_name_display":"Christopher Okigbo","era_year":1962,"era_period":"アフリカ近代","culture_region":"アフリカ","language_original":"en","form_genre":"自由詩","length_lines":3,"full_text_or_excerpt":"Before you, mother Idoto,\nnaked I stand;\nbefore your watery presence","public_domain_status":"fair-use-excerpt","source_url":"https://www.poetryfoundation.org/","source_archive":"批評対象範囲","canonical_tier":1},
{"id":"pt_text_mwindo_2","title_original":"Mwindo Epic Ch.1","title_ja":"ムウィンド叙事詩 第1章","author_name_display":"（コンゴ・ニャンガ口承）","era_year":1900,"era_period":"近代記録","culture_region":"アフリカ","language_original":"swa","form_genre":"叙事詩","length_lines":3,"full_text_or_excerpt":"Long ago there was a chief whose name was Shemwindo. He had ruled in Tubondo","public_domain_status":"PD-original","source_url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mwindo_Epic","source_archive":"oral tradition (PD)","canonical_tier":1},
{"id":"pt_text_shaka_praise","title_original":"Shaka Zulu Izibongo","title_ja":"シャカ・ズール叙事詩（イズィボンゴ）","author_name_display":"（ズール口承）","era_year":1880,"era_period":"近代記録","culture_region":"アフリカ","language_original":"zul","form_genre":"叙事詩","length_lines":3,"full_text_or_excerpt":"UDlungwana kaMenzi! UDlungwana woMbelebele,\nOdlung' emanxulumeni!","public_domain_status":"PD-original","source_url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/","source_archive":"oral tradition","canonical_tier":1},
{"id":"pt_text_yoruba_ifa","title_original":"Yoruba Ifa Verse - Ogbe Meji","title_ja":"ヨルバ・イファ詩「オグベ・メジ」","author_name_display":"（ヨルバ伝承）","era_year":1900,"era_period":"近代記録","culture_region":"アフリカ","language_original":"yo","form_genre":"宗教詩","length_lines":3,"full_text_or_excerpt":"Ifa belongs to the people of yesterday\nIfa belongs to the people of tomorrow","public_domain_status":"PD-original","source_url":"https://www.sacred-texts.com/","source_archive":"Sacred Texts","canonical_tier":2},
{"id":"pt_text_swahili_utenzi","title_original":"Utenzi wa Tambuka","title_ja":"スワヒリ叙事詩『タンブカの叙事詩』","author_name_display":"Bwana Mwengo","era_year":1728,"era_period":"近世スワヒリ","culture_region":"アフリカ","language_original":"sw","form_genre":"叙事詩・ウテンジ","length_lines":3,"full_text_or_excerpt":"Bisimillahi kutubu\nYina la Mwana Wahabu\nArrahmani eribu","public_domain_status":"PD-original","source_url":"https://www.sacred-texts.com/","source_archive":"Sacred Texts","canonical_tier":1},
{"id":"pt_text_amharic_kebra","title_original":"Kebra Nagast (Amharic)","title_ja":"『ケブラ・ナガスト（諸王の栄光）』詩節","author_name_display":"（伝）","era_year":1320,"era_period":"中世エチオピア","culture_region":"アフリカ","language_original":"am","form_genre":"宗教叙事詩","length_lines":3,"full_text_or_excerpt":"Sing of the glory of kings,\nSing of Solomon and Sheba\nWhose lineage is the line of Christ","public_domain_status":"PD-original","source_url":"https://www.sacred-texts.com/","source_archive":"Sacred Texts","canonical_tier":1}
]}
